-- title:
--   Every listed vertex has a unique first root
-- statement:
--   Let $(H_e)_{e\in E}$ be a hypergraph on $V$ with finitely many labels, and let $\mathbb P_p$ be the product law of independent hyperedge states with $\mathbb P(\omega_e=1)=p_e$. Write $\mathcal C^\omega_D(x)$ for the cluster of $x$ using open hyperedges disjoint from $D$, and $\mathcal C^\omega_D(S)$ for the union over $x\in S$. The mean after deletion is $m_W(F)=\mathbb E_p\,F(\mathcal C_W(s))$. For listed vertices $x_1,\dots,x_n$, the first root of $x_i$ is the first $x_k$ whose cluster (no deletion) contains $x_i$ and avoids all earlier $x_j$, $j<k$. The column of an observable $F$ is $\mathrm{col}_k(F)_i=\mathbb E_p\bigl[\mathbf 1\{x_k\text{ is the first root of }x_i\}\,F(\mathcal C(x_k))\bigr]$, the base matrix is $B_{ik}=\mathrm{col}_k(\mathbf 1)_i$, and $\mathrm{coeff}_k(F)=B^{-1}\mathrm{col}_k(F)$. For every configuration $\omega$, deleted set $D$ and index $i$, there is exactly one $k$ such that $x_k$ is the first root of $x_i$:
--   $$
--   \exists!\,k:\ \mathcal C_D(x_k)\cap\{x_j:j<k\}=\varnothing\ \text{and}\ x_k\leftrightarrow x_i .
--   $$
--
--   So the first-root events for $k=1,\dots,n$ partition the probability space for each fixed $i$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Probability/CriticalZ3/HyperedgeComparison.lean#L292-L311

